  "name": "harness-runs",
  "about": "A `coder:` node's harness runs, as child spans under their entry (`docs/trace.md` §7.6, §12.5, PRD resolved q57). Two runs on one entry, which is what a `retry:` ladder leaves behind: the first failed and carries its turns, its tool events and the error that ended it, and the second answered. Between them they reach every optional field of the record — usage per turn on one harness and a cost rollup in money on the other, the three-member tool vocabulary, and the harness-tagged extras.",
